{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0GEX", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$$\np : \\mathcal{S} \\longrightarrow (\\Sch/S)_h\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Sh(U_\\etale)$", "MATH_0005": "$U$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-h-descent-etale-sheaves}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3865c0a0c47121e978039332e42b2b2cb78dae36eed4ea1369ec0399f4370ab5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e2ae194eaf507212fd711c0c1234acb0efedef36172c088c391807e5af9c4cc5", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Then the category fibred in groupoids\n<MATH_0002>\nwhose fibre category over <MATH_0003> is the category <MATH_0004>\nof sheaves on the small <ACCENT_0001>tale site of <MATH_0005> is a stack in groupoids.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:265ba87ba31662282b526b94f5a1706c30c53f0dab5ee260f691766c51b39dfd", "unit_id": "tag:0GF5:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0GEX", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{X \\to Y\\}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{flat-lemma-refine-check-h-stack}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-lemma-glue-sheaves}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-glue-etale-sheaf-fppf-cover}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-glue-etale-sheaf-proper-surjective}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-glue-etale-sheaf-modification}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0005": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0006": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a04bec85bac79fafd714c3b56e4e759c69ee18330db55c5d2c4a707bb833307b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1357257b65e5e194f56b8a4412cb04f6cfb7392b67db46a50031fe245c744e4a", "source_text": "To prove the lemma we will check conditions (1), (2), and (3) of\nMore on Flatness, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nCondition (1) holds because we have glueing for sheaves (and\nZariski coverings are <ACCENT_0001>tale coverings). See\nSites, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nTo see condition (2), suppose that <MATH_0001> is a surjective,\nflat, proper morphism of finite presentation over <MATH_0002> with <MATH_0003> affine.\nThen we have descent for <MATH_0004> by either\nLemma <REF_0003> or\nLemma <REF_0004>.\n\n<STRUCT_0005><STRUCT_0006>\nCondition (3) follows immediately from the more general\nLemma <REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e170beeb47a898ef272f91ec759a479be0ce6b8eece9ce1a8c064425270caf5c", "unit_id": "tag:0GF5:proof"}
